<section class="about-positioning">
  <div class="about-shell about-story">
    <div class="about-positioning-copy">
      <p class="about-lead">Drawing led me to design.</p>
      <p>I started with illustration, painting for my daughters, creating paintings in the snow and trying different techniques. The turning point came when I realised that a design on screen could respond and come alive. Colour, typography and motion were no longer confined to a static image; suddenly, they could guide people and tell a product’s story.</p>
      <p>Traditional drawing teaches me to notice atmosphere, colour and detail. My experience in accounting gave me precision, patience and the need to understand a structure thoroughly before I begin to change it.</p>
      <p>Outside work, I look for colour inspiration outdoors, especially in autumn. I unwind with a good book and coffee. In video games, I am drawn to the way visuals, music, interaction and story come together. I still regularly return to making things by hand, together with my daughters.</p>
      <a class="about-inline-cta" href="{{ '/art/' | url }}">Explore the art portfolio <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="about-method">
  <div class="about-shell">
    <div class="about-section-heading"><p class="about-eyebrow">How I work</p><h2>From a problem to a usable solution.</h2></div>
    <ol class="about-steps">
      <li><span class="about-step-number">01</span><div><h3>Find the core</h3><p>Through research, interviews and competitive analysis, I test what people actually need and where the real problem lies.</p></div></li>
      <li><span class="about-step-number">02</span><div><h3>Define the direction</h3><p>I turn insights into information architecture, user flows and decisions that give the product a clear structure.</p></div></li>
      <li><span class="about-step-number">03</span><div><h3>Put it into practice</h3><p>I develop the direction into an interface, visual system and prototype. I test the result and prepare it for development.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

